eegvis is a hard fork in *purpose* of N-Nieto/Inner_Speech_Dataset
(https://github.com/N-Nieto/Inner_Speech_Dataset), which accompanies:

  Nieto, N., Peterson, V., Rufiner, H. L., Kamienkowski, J. E., & Spies, R. (2022).
  Thinking out loud, an open-access EEG-based BCI dataset for inner speech recognition.
  Scientific Data, 9, 52. https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-022-01147-2

That upstream repository is GPL-3. This package stays GPL-3.

This project is not dataset reproduction, not a 4-class inner-speech decoder, and
is not affiliated with Nieto et al. Algorithms here are original Python
implementations of visualization methods (CWT scalograms, rank-based
discriminability, sensor voting, SPD / Riemannian embeddings) with a
dataset-agnostic core. Nieto 2022 is the first adapter and demo.

Do not vendor Lawhern EEGNet or copy upstream MATLAB/Python_Processing into
this package. MATLAB memos in the parent tree are reference only.
